WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:02.935
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.337
We hope you're all
doing well tonight.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.671
And now, if you don't mind,
we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:07.573
First Lady Dr. Jill Biden

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.909
yesterday unveiled
a new postage stamp

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.679
that honors former
First Lady Nancy Reagan.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.615
The stamp will be very helpful
when you need to figure out

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:19.018
which birthday card
came from your grandparents.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.153
"Let's see.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:24.057
Flower, flower, Snoopy,
gay pride, oh!

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.925
Here we go."

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.994
Transportation Secretary
Pete Buttigieg

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:30.329
announced yesterday that
he has tested positive

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.532
for a breakthrough case
of the coronavirus.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.735
Unfortunately, he's still not
old enough for the vaccine.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.571
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.874
According to reports, former
President Trump's advisors

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:45.444
are divided on if Trump should
announce his re-election
campaign

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.881
before this year's
midterm elections or wait

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.683
so he does not take attention
away from other candidates.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.586
Oh, 'cause he'd hate
stealing attention.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.054
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:58.458
Trump's like a bridesmaid who
keeps mentioning in her speech

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.293
that it's her half-birthday.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.930
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.666
According to reports,
former President Trump

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.468
may launch his re-election
campaign on July 4th,

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.437
so step aside, dogs!

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.306
It's our turn to hate that day!

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.542
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.944
That's a good --
That's a very good

00:01:18.944 --> 00:01:21.080
"scared of a fireworks" dog,
right there.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.315
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.050
That's how you say it,
"a fireworks," right?

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.351
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.553
'Cause it sounded weird,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.021
but that's definitely
the way you say it.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:32.358
The sixth installment of
the dinosaur sci fi series

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.959
called
"Jurassic World: Dominion"

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:35.628
will be released this Friday
in theaters.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.097
Man, if that series goes on
any longer,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:40.266
they're gonna have to
include mammals.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.468
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.637
"The horses are out!"

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.773
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:50.276
Lawmakers in New York
recently passed

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.378
the so-called
Stop the Chop Act,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.546
which will allow residents
to sue companies

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.048
for excessive helicopter noise.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.718
So now, New York residents
will only have to deal with

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.053
noise from garbage trucks,
street sweepers,

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:02.855
ambulances, weed whackers,
leaf blowers,

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:06.092
and people screaming when a rat
pops its head out of a bodega.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.027
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.665
And finally, a guinea pig
in Hungary named Molly

00:02:13.665 --> 00:02:16.669
was recently honored with the
Guinness World Record

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.505
for most basketball slam dunks
in 30 seconds.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:22.841
But before you get too excited,
full disclosure,

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:26.846
apparently the rim was only set
at 9 feet, 6 inches.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.048
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.786
You know,
I was a little concerned

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.455
that that was our closer.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.623
Yeah.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.858
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.526
But you know what,
then I thought,

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:41.594
trust the process.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.030
Baze knows.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.298
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.401
I don't know why.
You know what, guys? Look.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.902
The important thing is,
we told that joke.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.437
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.039
We had the courage to tell it.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.475
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.876
That was a monologue, everybody!

00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:00.546
We have a fantastic

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:01.548
show for you tonight.

